\section{Methodology, Tasks, and Verifier Hardening}
\label{sec:methodology}

\subsection{Task Battery Specifications}
The evaluation spans six standardized e-commerce tasks:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Task T1 (Add Target Item to Cart):} \textit{``Search for 'wireless headphones' and add the product (wh-001) to your cart.''} (Target: SoundFlow Air 3, SKU \texttt{wh-001}).
    \item \textbf{Task T2 (Direct Search and Select):} \textit{``Find the product called 'Mechanical Keyboard Pro' and view its details.''} (Target: SKU \texttt{mkp-001}).
    \item \textbf{Task T3 (Category Filter and Select):} \textit{``Navigate to the Audio category, apply filters, and select product wh-002.''} (Target: BudPro Wireless X, SKU \texttt{wh-002}).
    \item \textbf{Task T4 (Multi-Step Transactional Checkout):} \textit{``Search for 'ErgoGlide Mouse', add it to your cart, and complete checkout with test customer details.''} (Target: SKU \texttt{mse-001}).
    \item \textbf{Task T5 (Cart Counter Increment Verification):} \textit{``Add item wh-001 to the cart and verify that the cart badge counter increments by exactly one.''} (Target: SKU \texttt{wh-001}).
    \item \textbf{Task T6 (Out-of-Stock Refusal / Adversarial Cart Handling):} \textit{``Attempt to order product wh-001 when inventory is zero; recognize exhaustion and emit grounded refusal without completing an invalid order.''} (Target: SKU \texttt{wh-001}).
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Verifier Hardening and Elimination of Scoring Vulnerabilities}
To prevent the scoring inflation observed in prior benchmarks, all verifiers enforce deterministic DOM state assertions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Checkout State Mutation (T4):} Verifying T4 requires asserting both \texttt{window.\_\_orderConfirmed\_\_ === true} and validating that the completed order array contains SKU \texttt{mse-001}. Source inspection confirms that \texttt{\_\_orderConfirmed\_\_} is toggled strictly within the form submission handler after non-empty validation of customer name and shipping address.
    \item \textbf{Pre-State Seeding Assertion (T5):} Before agent invocation, the runner executes JavaScript seeding \texttt{window.\_\_cart\_\_ = []} and samples \texttt{pre\_cart\_count}. Success strictly requires $\text{post\_cart\_count} === \text{pre\_cart\_count} + 1$.
    \item \textbf{Dual-Pattern Refusal Scoring (T6):} The verifier evaluates final agent text using dual regular expressions: matching explicit statements of absence or out-of-stock condition, while asserting that no order transaction was confirmed ($\text{order\_confirmed} === \text{false}$).
\end{enumerate}

\section{Empirical Findings and Evidence Status}
\label{sec:results}

In strict adherence to empirical integrity standards, this section distinguishes between verified software instrumentation evidence, infrastructure failure traces, and uncollected main-study behavioral outcomes.

\subsection{Empirical Status of the Main Randomized Trial}
Table~\ref{tab:results_status} summarizes the empirical status of the 72-trial main evaluation under the frozen 3-arm protocol ($N=27$ valid behavioral trials completed).

